  "$comment": "Shared conformance cases for the discriminator. Python is authoritative: tools/gen-fixtures.py runs these through the real engine and writes expected.json. The browser port in apps/web/lib/discriminator is checked against that file by tools/check-parity.mjs, so the interactive playground can never quietly disagree with the engine that actually scores the archive. Cases are chosen to pin the gates, not to look impressive.",
